; --lot-prices keeps a sale written {=price}, without the lot's date,
; apart from the floating lot bought at that price: the "=" marker is part
; of a lot's identity (#1454), and a posting that names a lot posts to the
; lot it names.
;
; The pounds are bought "@ 1.4 EUR", which makes the floating lot
; {1.40 EUR} [2008/01/01], and sold as {=1.4 EUR}, which names a fixated
; lot of the same price: Assets:Pounds goes short that lot and keeps the
; floating one.  Reports without lot details still let the sale close the
; purchase (bal below; C0212EAC.test pins reg), and --lots lists the two
; lots apart.  --lot-prices used to drop the sale's marker when it reduced
; each lot to its price, so sale and purchase became one lot (which was
; then marked fixated), the pounds cancelled and the grand total was 0.
; It now keeps the marker and leaves the purchase's lot floating, so it
; lists both lots as --lots does, minus the purchase date, and the grand
; total carries them.  A sale written {1.4 EUR} closes the floating lot in
; this report.

2008/01/01 Buy pounds
    Assets:Pounds          5.00 GBP @ 1.4 EUR
    Assets:Euros

2009/01/01 Sell the pounds bought at 1.4 EUR
    Assets:Pounds         -5.00 GBP {=1.4 EUR} @ 1.5 EUR
    Assets:Euros           7.50 EUR
    Income:Gain

test bal
            0.50 EUR  Assets:Euros
           -0.50 EUR  Income:Gain
--------------------
                   0
end test

test bal --lots
                        0.50 EUR
           -5.00 GBP {=1.40 EUR}
5.00 GBP {1.40 EUR} [2008/01/01]  Assets
            0.50 EUR    Euros
           -5.00 GBP {=1.40 EUR}
5.00 GBP {1.40 EUR} [2008/01/01]    Pounds
           -0.50 EUR  Income:Gain
--------------------
           -5.00 GBP {=1.40 EUR}
5.00 GBP {1.40 EUR} [2008/01/01]
end test

test bal --lot-prices
             0.50 EUR
  5.00 GBP {1.40 EUR}
-5.00 GBP {=1.40 EUR}  Assets
            0.50 EUR    Euros
  5.00 GBP {1.40 EUR}
-5.00 GBP {=1.40 EUR}    Pounds
           -0.50 EUR  Income:Gain
--------------------
  5.00 GBP {1.40 EUR}
-5.00 GBP {=1.40 EUR}
end test
